@* The real pairing: a gradient edge around a Card, plus a restyled edge to show that Class wins
   over the recipe. A Card's own bg-card covers the default bg-background underneath, so the
   default Surface stays correct without being told. *@
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-start gap-6">
    <GradientBorder Class="w-72">
        <Card>
            <CardHeader>
                <CardTitle>Deploy preview</CardTitle>
                <CardDescription>build-4821 · staging</CardDescription>
            </CardHeader>
            <CardContent>
                <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                    214 files changed. Ready to review.
                </p>
            </CardContent>
        </Card>
    </GradientBorder>

    @* Same component, a different gradient — no parameters involved. tailwind-merge replaces
       the recipe's colour-stop and gradient-direction classes with these. *@
    <GradientBorder Class="w-72 bg-gradient-to-br from-destructive/70 via-accent to-primary/70">
        <div class="bg-card p-4">
            <p class="font-medium">Quota nearly spent</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                92% of this month's requests used. The warning is the text above, not the edge.
            </p>
        </div>
    </GradientBorder>
</div>
